## Local environment — do not guess this

This Mac runs **PostgreSQL 17 via Homebrew on `localhost:5432`**. It is already
installed and running.

- **Never start Docker for pytest.** Docker Compose is optional here and is not
  used for tests. If a DB connection fails, fix the URL or the role — do not
  reach for a container.
- **Always run pytest through the venv binary**: `.venv/bin/pytest -q`. A bare
  `python3 -m pytest` picks up the wrong interpreter and fails on missing
  packages; `tests/conftest.py` will reject it.
- The suite shares one test database. **One pytest run at a time** — never start
  a second while one is going.

```bash
cd backend
export DATABASE_ADMIN_URL='postgresql+psycopg://shoaib@localhost:5432/postgres'
.venv/bin/pytest -q
```

Full green light (all of it, before claiming done) is in `AGENT_GUARDRAILS.md §1`
— it includes `npx eslint .` over the whole tree and a real `next build`, both of
which catch things vitest and tsc do not.

Slice gate: Characterize → Audit → Test → Fix → API → Verify → ROADMAP → Commit/tag.

FUTURE_IDEAS.md is out of scope until promoted to Decisions.
